; A GRAPH — the extensional presentation. β-tab looks an element up when the
; expect: 0 10 30 60 150 150 150 150 150
; index is a literal and leaves the application alone when it is not, so the
; same text `(a i)` is an indexing whether it reduces here or reaches a backend
; (tables.md §3.1).
;
; `n` selects dynamically, so nothing folds and the table has to exist.
(def run (fn (n)
  (let (array 10 20 30 40 50) (fn (a)
    (loop ((acc 0) (i 0))
      (>= i (len a))  acc
      (>= i n)        acc
      else             (again (+ acc (a i)) (+ i 1)))))))
